---
title: Reusable assets
description: Backgrounds, overlays, frames, photo frames, red strips, lower thirds, arrows, stickers and the LUTs — PNGs you can drop into KineMaster, PicsArt, CapCut, Canva or Pixelmator, in horizontal (1920 × 1080) and vertical (1080 × 1920).
eyebrow: Concept · Make
---
<p>Everything here is made in the system's own look — ink, white, one red — and carries no words, so it fits any post. Light versions first; a handful in red. Each file comes in <b>H</b> (1920 × 1080, for YouTube and thumbnails) and <b>V</b> (1080 × 1920, for Reels, Shorts and stories); square ones work in both. Free to use in your own videos and posts.</p>
<p><a class="im-btn im-btn-ink" href="/assets/kit/im-mobile-kit.zip" download>Download everything (.zip)</a> &nbsp; <a href="/concept/mobile/">How to use them on your phone →</a></p>
<h2 id="how">How each kind goes on</h2>
<div class="im-table-scroll"><table>
<thead><tr><th>File</th><th>In KineMaster</th><th>In PicsArt</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Background</td><td>Use as the first clip (Media › pick the PNG), then put your photo/video on a Layer above</td><td>Start a new project from the PNG</td></tr>
<tr><td>Overlay (transparent PNG)</td><td>Layer › Media › the PNG, stretch to full frame, Opacity 20–60%</td><td>Add Photo › the PNG, Blend: Normal, Opacity 20–60%</td></tr>
<tr><td>Frame, photo frame, strip, lower third</td><td>Layer › Media › the PNG above your photo</td><td>Add Photo › the PNG above your photo; for a photo frame, put the photo under the hole</td></tr>
<tr><td>Arrow, sticker</td><td>Layer › Media, resize and rotate like a sticker</td><td>Sticker › My stickers › upload, or Add Photo</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>

